   "text": "The structure is trovafloxacin. It is a 1,8-naphthyridin-4-one-3-carboxylic acid with a 2,4-difluorophenyl group on N1, a fluorine at C6, and a 6-amino-3-azabicyclo[3.1.0]hexane attached through its nitrogen at C7.\n\n**Core and substituents**\n- The bicyclic core has two ring nitrogens (N1 and N8). N1 carries the 2,4-difluorophenyl group.\n- C3 carries the carboxylic acid and C4 is the ketone.\n- C6 carries the fluorine, and C7 carries the bicyclic amine nitrogen.\n\n**Bicyclic amine**\n- It is a pyrrolidine fused to a cyclopropane, and the cyclopropane carbon outside the pyrrolidine bears the NH2.\n- The two ring-fusion carbons each have an H drawn as a wedge, so these two centres get stereo marks.\n- The carbon bearing NH2 is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo mark.\n\nI worked out the @/@@ marks for the two fusion carbons from the wedge geometry in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: NC1[C@@H]2CN(c3nc4n(cc(C(O)=O)c(=O)c4cc3F)-c3ccc(F)cc3F)C[C@H]12"
